# Default owners for the entire repository.
#
# Review is not a formality here. This code launches messages to real
# respondents and handles the identifiers they give up in return, and the
# defects that have actually reached production were all of one kind: they
# reported success at the moment they failed. A second reader is the control
# for that.
* @PovertyAction/grds

# The encryption scheme has two implementations that must agree forever - one
# Python, one JavaScript running inside Twilio. A change to either that is not
# mirrored in the other makes collected data unreadable, and nothing surfaces
# that until decryption is attempted, after the round.
/src/requests_to_twilio/crypto.py      @PovertyAction/grds
/src/requests_to_twilio/decryptor.py   @PovertyAction/grds
/twilio_functions/encrypt_fields.js    @PovertyAction/grds
